Runs the Checkmk agent on OPNsense, so that a Checkmk server can
monitor the firewall like any other host. Checkmk's built-in checks
evaluate the agent data: CPU load and utilization, memory, file
systems and ZFS, network interfaces, TCP connections, processes,
uptime and NTP.

Features:

* Enable the agent in the GUI under Services: Checkmk Agent
* The agent listens on TCP port 6556 (IPv4 and IPv6)
* Optional symmetric encryption, compatible with Checkmk's rule
  "Symmetric encryption (Linux, Windows)"
* Host labels "opnsense" and "opnsense/version" for Checkmk rules
* Agent plugins for the SSH daemon configuration and logged-in users
* Own agent plugins and local checks in
  /usr/local/lib/check_mk_agent/plugins and .../local

Use firewall rules to allow port 6556 only from the Checkmk server.

For OPNsense-specific data from the REST API (firmware and updates,
services, SMART), combine this plugin with the Checkmk special agent
"opnsense" (link below).

